{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/july-topics-packet.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"id\": \"t01\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will U.S. federal agencies obligate in AI-related spending in calendar/fiscal 2026, and how much in new AI-related contract awards will be recorded?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The total AI-related spending obligated by U.S. federal agencies in 2026 (reported at $7.2 billion so far, versus $675 million in 2024) and the value of potential AI contract awards (reported at $91.8 billion, versus $4.6 billion in 2024).\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar/fiscal 2026; settled by year-end 2026 U.S. federal procurement data (e.g., USAspending.gov) reporting total AI-related obligations and contract awards. Set from the item's 2026 obligations figure ($7.2 billion) and potential-awards figure ($91.8 billion).\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"U.S. federal procurement records — USAspending.gov and agency AI budget/award disclosures — reporting total AI-related obligations and contract awards for calendar/fiscal 2026.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-14\",\n   \"title\": \"FBI Issues RFI for AI Supercomputers Featuring Nvidia B300 GPUs and Google TPUs\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks two figures—2026 AI-related federal spending obligations and potential AI contract awards—and neither is identified as the main figure.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic names two figures—AI-related federal spending obligations and potential AI contract awards—and neither is identified as the main one.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks two figures—total AI-related spending obligated and the value of potential AI contract awards—and neither is identified as the main figure.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t02\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the combined data center capital expenditures of the 'big four' AI hyperscalers for calendar 2026 come in near the ~$650 billion the item reports they plan to spend?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' aggregated calendar-2026 data center capital expenditure versus the ~$650 billion plan reported in the item, with Nvidia's own projection of ~$1 trillion for 2027 as the forward reference.\",\n   \"period\": \"Full-year calendar 2026, checked against the hyperscalers' capex disclosures in their Q4 2026 earnings reports (reported roughly January–February 2027); the item gives no release date, so the check date is set by the companies' own year-end reporting.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The capital expenditure line in each of the big four AI hyperscalers' quarterly earnings reports, summed at their Q4 2026 reports.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-04\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditure be for calendar 2026, as measured by summing the capex lines in their Q4 2026 earnings reports?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be for calendar 2026, as measured by the sum of their capital-expenditure lines in their Q4 2026 earnings reports?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend in aggregate on data center capital expenditures during calendar 2026, according to the capital expenditure lines in their Q4 2026 earnings reports?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 550,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 550,000,000,000 USD to below 625,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 625,000,000,000 USD to below 675,000,000,000 USD: from 625,000,000,000 USD to below 675,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\\")\",\n     \"from 675,000,000,000 USD to below 750,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"750,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t03\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will China's government permit NVIDIA to sell its H200 AI chips to Chinese customers, lifting its current block, by NVIDIA's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A Chinese government/regulator decision allowing H200 sales in China, evidenced by an official Chinese decision or by NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments/revenue to Chinese customers.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-01-31 (NVIDIA's current fiscal year-end; set because the item reports a pending regulatory decision with no date of its own)\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"An official Chinese government or regulator decision permitting H200 sales into China, or NVIDIA's disclosure of H200 shipments/revenue to Chinese customers in its FY2027 Form 10-K or quarterly filings.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will China's government or a regulator permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips to Chinese customers by 2027-01-31, as shown by an official Chinese decision or NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments or revenue to Chinese customers?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: By 2027-01-31, an official Chinese government or regulator decision permits H200 sales to Chinese customers, or NVIDIA confirms H200 shipments or revenue to Chinese customers.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The Chinese government or a Chinese regulator formally denies permission for H200 sales to Chinese customers or formally prohibits those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will China permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips to Chinese customers by 2027-01-31, as evidenced by an official Chinese decision or NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments or revenue to Chinese customers?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: By 2027-01-31, an official Chinese government or regulator decision permits H200 sales to Chinese customers, or NVIDIA confirms H200 shipments or revenue to Chinese customers.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The Chinese government or a Chinese regulator formally denies permission for H200 sales to Chinese customers or formally prohibits those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will China officially permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips to Chinese customers by 2027-01-31, as established by an official Chinese decision or NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments or revenue to those customers?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: By 2027-01-31, China officially permits NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips to Chinese customers, or NVIDIA confirms H200 shipments or revenue to those customers in a filing.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-02 and before 2027-01-31, the Chinese government or a Chinese regulator formally denies permission for H200 sales into China or formally decides to maintain or impose a prohibition on those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t04\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will France's competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets and issue a decision (fines or remedies) by Nvidia's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A final decision by the French competition authority on its antitrust probe into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-01-31 (Nvidia's current fiscal year-end; set because the item reports a pending regulatory decision 'nearing a conclusion' with no date of its own)\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The French competition authority's published final decision/remedies on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-09, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a final decision. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-09, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a final decision. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-09, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws its investigation without publishing a final decision. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t05\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How large will NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments be at its next annual report, and could that obligation pressure its cash or credit position if AI demand disappoints?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Total dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments disclosed at its next annual report, against the ~$119 billion the item cites as the current reference.\",\n   \"period\": \"Next annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027, reported ~February 2027); set as the next annual report because the supply commitments are presented as already undertaken/outstanding.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's Form 10-K purchase commitments / contractual obligations disclosure and interim Form 10-Q updates.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What total dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments outstanding at the end of FY2027 will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 90,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 90,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"$119B in supply commitments\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What total dollar amount of NVIDIA supply purchase commitments will be disclosed in its Form 10-K for FY2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 100,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 100,000,000,000 USD to below 115,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 115,000,000,000 USD to below 125,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Nvidia's $119B in supply commitments\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 125,000,000,000 USD to below 140,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 140,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What total dollar amount of NVIDIA supply purchase commitments will NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 annual report, as measured in the report’s purchase commitments / contractual obligations disclosure?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 90,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 90,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Nvidia's $119B in supply commitments\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t06\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How large will US federal AI spending obligations be in calendar 2026, and how much in potential contract awards, as a demand pool for Nvidia's AI accelerators?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Total US federal AI spending obligations in calendar 2026, against the $7.2 billion reported as reached and the $91.8 billion in potential contract awards.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; set as the year the item reports for federal AI spending obligations, checked against year-end 2026 federal procurement data (USAspending.gov/SAM.gov).\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Year-end 2026 federal procurement data on AI obligations and contract awards (USAspending.gov, SAM.gov), compared with the $7.2 billion obligations and $91.8 billion potential awards reported in the item.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-14\",\n   \"title\": \"FBI Issues RFI for AI Supercomputers Featuring Nvidia B300 GPUs and Google TPUs\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What were total US federal AI spending obligations in calendar 2026, according to year-end 2026 federal procurement data from USAspending.gov and SAM.gov?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 3,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 3,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"$7.2 billion\\\")\",\n     \"from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"15,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What total amount of US federal AI spending obligations will year-end 2026 federal procurement data (USAspending.gov/SAM.gov) show for calendar 2026?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 5,760,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 5,760,000,000 USD to below 7,200,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 7,200,000,000 USD to below 8,640,000,000 USD: from 7,200,000,000 USD to below 8,640,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"obligated funds reaching $7.2 billion in 2026\\\")\",\n     \"from 8,640,000,000 USD to below 10,800,000,000 USD\",\n     \"10,800,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"no ladder: refused\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t07\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How large is NVIDIA's equity investment in Intel, and will the $5 billion stake be completed and held at that level as disclosed in NVIDIA's filings?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount of NVIDIA's equity stake in Intel and whether the reported $5 billion investment is completed, as disclosed in NVIDIA's next annual report and any related 8-K / Schedule 13D-G filings.\",\n   \"period\": \"Next annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027, reported ~February 2027); set as the next annual report because the item presents the $5 billion as an equity investment/commitment allocated to Intel, i.e. a sized stake tracked by its amount at that report.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027, together with any 8-K or Schedule 13D/13G filings disclosing the size and closing of the Intel equity stake.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   \"title\": \"Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What dollar amount of NVIDIA's equity stake in Intel will NVIDIA disclose as of FY2027 year-end (January 31, 2027), as stated in its FY2027 Form 10-K and any related 8-K or Schedule 13D/13G filings?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 4,500,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 4,500,000,000 USD to below 4,900,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 4,900,000,000 USD to below 5,100,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"$5 billion equity investment\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 5,100,000,000 USD to below 5,500,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 5,500,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What dollar amount of its equity investment in Intel does NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K and related 8-K or Schedule 13D/13G filings?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 4,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 4,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 6,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"NVIDIA’s $5 billion equity investment\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 6,000,000,000 USD to below 7,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 7,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What dollar amount of NVIDIA’s equity stake in Intel will NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 annual report and related filings?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 4,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 4,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 5,500,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"$5 billion equity investment\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 5,500,000,000 USD to below 6,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 6,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t08\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"What share of Chinese companies' AI accelerator spending will go to domestic suppliers over the 12 months following July 2026, versus the 46% planned in the Bloomberg Intelligence survey?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The realized share of Chinese enterprises' AI accelerator budget captured by domestic suppliers (Huawei, Hygon, Cambricon and others) over the 12 months from mid-2026, measured against the 46% planned and the 30% current level.\",\n   \"period\": \"The 12 months from the survey's release on 2026-07-07 (to mid-2027); settled when follow-up survey or market-share data covering that period are published.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"A follow-up Bloomberg Intelligence survey of Chinese AI buyers or third-party China AI accelerator market data (e.g. IDC/Canalys vendor shipment and share data) covering mid-2026 to mid-2027.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Chinese firms leave Nvidia for local AI suppliers, survey shows\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The figure covers a rolling 12-month period, and neither the topic nor the item gives the publication day of the follow-up survey or market data that would settle it.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The figure covers a rolling 12-month period, and neither the topic nor the item gives the publication day of the data that will settle it.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked figure covers a rolling 12-month period, not one fiscal or calendar year, and neither the topic nor the item gives the day the follow-up survey or market-share data covering that period will be published.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t09\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will commodity DRAM (and by extension graphics memory) contract prices rise further through calendar 2026, deepening the memory shortage that is raising GPU makers' memory input costs?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Direction and magnitude of commodity DRAM/graphics memory contract prices over calendar 2026, and whether the shortage that has forced NVIDIA to revive an older graphics card persists through the year.\",\n   \"period\": \"Full-year calendar 2026 — the item states the DRAM crisis 'intensifies in 2026'; checked against Q4 2026 DRAM contract price releases (TrendForce/DRAMeXchange) and memory makers' Q4 2026 results, reported roughly January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"TrendForce/DRAMeXchange quarterly DRAM contract price releases and Micron/SK Hynix/Samsung quarterly reports covering Q3–Q4 2026.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-05\",\n   \"title\": \"NVIDIA’s RTX 3060 12 GB Graphics Card Comeback Proves Just How Bad Things Are For The PC Gaming Market\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What will the percentage change be in commodity DRAM contract prices from the end of 2025 to the Q4 2026 price level, as established by TrendForce/DRAMeXchange contract-price releases?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 0 percent\",\n     \"from 0 percent to below 10 percent\",\n     \"from 10 percent to below 20 percent: from 10 percent to below 20 percent (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 20 percent to below 40 percent\",\n     \"40 percent or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What will the percentage change in commodity DRAM contract prices from Q4 2025 to Q4 2026 be, as shown in TrendForce/DRAMeXchange Q4 2026 contract-price releases?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 0 percent\",\n     \"from 0 percent to below 10 percent\",\n     \"from 10 percent to below 30 percent: from 10 percent to below 30 percent (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 30 percent to below 60 percent\",\n     \"60 percent or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What will the percentage change in commodity DRAM contract prices be from Q4 2025 to Q4 2026, as shown in TrendForce/DRAMeXchange contract-price releases?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 0 percent\",\n     \"from 0 percent to below 10 percent\",\n     \"from 10 percent to below 20 percent: from 10 percent to below 20 percent (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 20 percent to below 40 percent\",\n     \"40 percent or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t10\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much credit support or guarantee exposure will NVIDIA have signed for AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model by 2027-12-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The amount of signed credit-support, guarantee, or similar credit-enhancement commitments NVIDIA discloses for AI cloud partners under the new model.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-12-31 (check date within 18 months of the 2026-07-01 item, for an unsigned obligation)\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's annual report/Form 10-K, 8-K, or other filing disclosures of guarantees, credit support, and commitments, and signed partner agreements.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   \"title\": \"NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What total amount in USD of credit-support, guarantee, or similar credit-enhancement commitments will NVIDIA have signed for AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model by 2027-12-31, as established by NVIDIA’s filings or signed partner agreements?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 100,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 100,000,000 USD to below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 10,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What total amount of credit-support, guarantee, or similar credit-enhancement commitments will NVIDIA have signed for AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model, as measured on 2027-12-31, according to NVIDIA's annual report, Form 10-K, Form 8-K, other filing disclosures, or signed partner agreements?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 15,000,000,000 USD to below 30,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 30,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What aggregate USD amount of credit-support, guarantee, or similar credit-enhancement commitments will NVIDIA have signed for AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model by 2027-12-31, as determined from signed partner agreements and NVIDIA filings?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 25,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t11\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will NVIDIA have outstanding in supply/purchase commitments at its next annual report?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply commitments (purchase and capacity commitments) disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K, versus the $119 billion cited in this item.\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, expected early 2027); the commitments are already undertaken, so they are tracked by their amount at the next annual report.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's FY2027 Form 10-K, which discloses supply commitments/purchase obligations in its contractual-obligations disclosure.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia’s Biggest Threat Is This: Everyone Is Desperate to Stop Paying Nvidia Prices.\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What dollar amount of NVIDIA’s supply, purchase and capacity commitments will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 90,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 90,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Supply commitments of $119 billion\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply and purchase/capacity commitments will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 95,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 95,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Supply commitments of $119 billion\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply commitments (purchase and capacity commitments) will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K contractual-obligations disclosure?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 95,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 95,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Supply commitments of $119 billion\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t12\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the French competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA's cloud-AI and GPU practices and impose remedies or fines, and by when?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether the French competition authority issues a decision (behavioral remedies, commitments or fines) closing its probe into alleged anti-competitive practices in NVIDIA's cloud-AI and GPU markets.\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's current fiscal year-end (late January 2027) — set as the check date for a pending regulatory decision the item dates only as 'nearing a conclusion'.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The French competition authority's published decision or announcement concluding/resolving its investigation into NVIDIA.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion resolving its investigation into NVIDIA by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or conclusion resolving its investigation into NVIDIA by January 31, 2027, whatever it finds.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion resolving it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or announcement concluding or resolving its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA's cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or announcement concluding or resolving its investigation into NVIDIA's cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027, whatever the decision finds.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 9, 2026, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or announcement concluding or resolving it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion resolving its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or conclusion resolving its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-09, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion resolving it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t13\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will China's government allow selected Chinese AI firms (including Alibaba Group Holding) to buy Nvidia H200 GPUs, and at what scale, replacing the current restriction that bars Chinese firms from purchasing the device?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Beijing implements its reported plan to permit selected Chinese companies to buy limited numbers of Nvidia H200 GPUs, the scale of permitted purchases, and any subsequent broadening or tightening versus the current restriction.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal year ending late January 2027 (reported ~February 2027); set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision, because the item gives no date for Beijing's authorisation.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Chinese government (State Council / Cyberspace Administration of China / Ministry of Commerce) official announcements and authorization lists on H200 purchases, plus Nvidia's disclosed China revenue and Alibaba's procurement/capex disclosures.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Game-changer? Why China is finally letting its AI firms buy the Nvidia H200\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will the Chinese government officially authorize selected Chinese AI firms, including Alibaba, to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: By January 31, 2027, the Chinese government officially authorizes selected Chinese AI firms, including Alibaba, to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 9, 2026, the Chinese government formally announces that it will not authorize selected Chinese AI firms to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs, or formally abandons the reported plan to authorize those purchases. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will China’s government officially authorize selected Chinese AI firms to buy Nvidia H200 GPUs by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: China’s government officially authorizes selected Chinese AI firms to buy Nvidia H200 GPUs by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 9, 2026, the Chinese government formally announces that it will not authorize selected Chinese AI firms to buy Nvidia H200 GPUs, or formally abandons the plan to authorize those purchases. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will the Chinese government officially authorize selected Chinese AI companies, including Alibaba, to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The Chinese government officially authorizes selected Chinese AI companies, including Alibaba, to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The Chinese government formally abandons the reported plan or officially decides against authorizing selected Chinese companies to purchase H200 GPUs. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t14\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory contract prices rise in calendar 2026, and what will the memory content of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin VR200 rack cost, now that memory is reported to be 25-30% of the rack bill of materials?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The direction and size of 2026 memory contract price increases and the memory cost per NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack (Morgan Stanley currently puts memory content at about $2 million per rack, up 435%), which bears on NVIDIA's per-rack cost/ASP economics and on hyperscaler AI-infrastructure spending.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026 — checked against memory contract price releases and NVIDIA/partner disclosures of rack bill-of-materials as Vera Rubin ramps during H2 2026.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Memory contract price data (e.g., TrendForce/DRAMeXchange DDR5, NAND and HBM contract prices) and NVIDIA/partner disclosures of the Vera Rubin rack BOM as it ships and ramps in Q3-Q4 2026.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic names two tracked figures—the 2026 memory contract price increases and memory cost per NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack—without identifying either as the main figure.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic names two tracked figures—the 2026 memory contract price increases and the memory cost per NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack—but neither is identified as the main one.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks two figures—the 2026 memory contract price increases and the memory cost per NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack—and names neither as the main figure.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t15\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will DRAM/HBM contract prices remain elevated through calendar 2027, extending the shortage that has raised GPU makers' memory input costs?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Direction and level of DRAM/HBM contract prices through calendar 2027, specifically whether they remain above 2026 levels or normalize as Micron's 2027/2028 outlook suggests.\",\n   \"period\": \"Full-year calendar 2027; checked against Q4 2027 DRAM contract price releases (TrendForce/DRAMeXchange) and memory makers' Q4 2027 results, reported roughly January 2028.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"TrendForce/DRAMeXchange quarterly and Q4 2027 DRAM contract price releases, plus Micron, Samsung and SK Hynix Q4 2027 results and supply commentary.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-12\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Skips New Gaming GPUs, Breaks 30-Year Streak [2026] - https://tech-insider.org/\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What will the percentage change in the calendar-2027 average DRAM/HBM contract-price level be versus calendar 2026, as determined from TrendForce/DRAMeXchange releases and memory makers’ Q4 2027 results?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-03-30\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below -20 percent\",\n     \"from -20 percent to below 0 percent\",\n     \"from 0 percent to below 20 percent: from 0 percent to below 20 percent (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 20 percent to below 50 percent\",\n     \"50 percent or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What will the average DRAM/HBM contract-price level in calendar 2027 be, measured as the percentage change from the calendar-2026 average, as determined from TrendForce/DRAMeXchange contract-price releases and memory makers’ Q4 2027 results and supply commentary?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-03-30\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below -10 percent\",\n     \"from -10 percent to below 0 percent\",\n     \"from 0 percent to below 10 percent: from 0 percent to below 10 percent (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 10 percent to below 30 percent\",\n     \"30 percent or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What will the year-over-year percentage change in DRAM/HBM contract prices be in Q4 2027 versus Q4 2026, as shown by TrendForce/DRAMeXchange’s Q4 2027 releases and memory makers’ Q4 2027 results?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-03-30\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below -10 percent\",\n     \"from -10 percent to below 0 percent\",\n     \"from 0 percent to below 15 percent: from 0 percent to below 15 percent (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 15 percent to below 35 percent\",\n     \"35 percent or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t16\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the spot price for an hour on an Nvidia H100 GPU continue to fall through calendar 2026, extending the drop from its May 2026 peak of about $3.20?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Direction of the H100 GPU hourly spot rental price through calendar 2026, specifically whether it remains below the ~$3.20/hour May 2026 peak and continues the steady decline.\",\n   \"period\": \"Year-end 2026; set as the check date for whether the H100 spot price remains below the May 2026 peak of about $3.20/hour, using Ornn/compute marketplace spot price data.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Ornn (or other GPU compute marketplace) spot price indices for Nvidia H100 hourly rentals, and cloud providers' GPU pricing disclosures through 2026.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia is a victim of the compute marketplace it created\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked matter is the spot rental price for Nvidia H100 GPU compute on marketplaces, which is not a figure of NVDA itself and is not covered by any listed theme.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked matter is the spot rental price of Nvidia H100 GPU compute, which is not covered by any of the listed themes; it is not a figure for Nvidia itself.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked matter is the spot rental price for Nvidia H100 GPU-hours on compute marketplaces. That is neither an Nvidia company figure nor a matter covered by the listed themes.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t17\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will the top U.S. hyperscalers spend on custom AI accelerators (ASIC/XPU chips such as those Marvell designs for Amazon and Microsoft) in calendar 2026, and how much AI-accelerator demand is bypassing NVIDIA GPUs?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The dollar volume of hyperscaler custom-ASIC purchases in calendar 2026 (as reflected in the ASIC vendors' custom AI silicon revenue) versus those hyperscalers' NVIDIA GPU purchases — a measure of how far AI compute is shifting from NVIDIA GPUs to custom silicon for inference.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026 (this calendar year relative to the 14 July 2026 item), checked against ASIC vendors' and hyperscalers' calendar-2026 disclosures in early 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Marvell's and Broadcom's disclosed custom AI silicon revenue for the four quarters of calendar 2026 (quarterly results and 10-K/10-Q filings) together with the top U.S. hyperscalers' capex and accelerator-mix commentary in their Q4 2026 earnings releases.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-14\",\n   \"title\": \"Move Over Nvidia, This Custom Chip Stock Could Be the Next Big Winner\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic names custom-ASIC purchases and NVIDIA GPU purchases as two figures to compare, but does not identify either as the single main figure being tracked.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What was the total USD amount of custom AI silicon revenue reflecting the top U.S. hyperscalers’ custom-ASIC purchases during calendar 2026, based on Marvell’s and Broadcom’s disclosures for the four quarters of 2026?\",\n    \"whose\": \"custom-silicon\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 10,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 15,000,000,000 USD to below 20,000,000,000 USD: from 15,000,000,000 USD to below 20,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 20,000,000,000 USD to below 30,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"30,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"How much custom-AI-accelerator revenue will Marvell and Broadcom disclose for calendar 2026, as a proxy for the top U.S. hyperscalers’ custom-ASIC purchases, in their 2026 results and filings?\",\n    \"whose\": \"custom-silicon\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 10,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 20,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 20,000,000,000 USD to below 30,000,000,000 USD: from 20,000,000,000 USD to below 30,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 30,000,000,000 USD to below 40,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"40,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t18\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026, and does the aggregate reach the ~$650 billion currently planned?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The combined 2026 data-center capex the four largest AI hyperscalers actually report/spend, versus the ~$650 billion currently planned and NVIDIA's ~$1 trillion projection for the following year.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026 — checked against the hyperscalers' reported full-year 2026 capex in their Q4 2026 earnings releases (early 2027).\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Quarterly capex disclosures and full-year 2026 capital-expenditure figures in the earnings releases of Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet and Meta.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-04\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"How much did Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet and Meta report spending on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026, as disclosed in their full-year 2026 earnings releases?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What will the combined data-center capital expenditures actually reported or spent by Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, and Meta be for calendar 2026, as disclosed in their full-year 2026 earnings releases?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"around $650 billion\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What will Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, and Meta's combined data-center capital expenditures actually reported or spent be for calendar 2026, according to their full-year 2026 capex disclosures in their Q4 2026 earnings releases?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t19\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will France's competition authority (Autorité de la concurrence) conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by issuing a formal decision — a statement of objections, fine or behavioural remedies — rather than closing the case without action?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A formal decision, or closure without action, by the French competition authority in its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's alleged anti-competitive practices in cloud-AI and GPU markets, including any fine or remedy imposed.\",\n   \"period\": \"Nvidia's fiscal year ending late January 2027 (FY2027, reported ~February 2027); set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision because the item gives no date beyond the authority's Thursday announcement.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The French competition authority's published decision/announcement concluding the investigation (and any statement of objections), plus Nvidia's disclosure of material legal proceedings in its 10-Q/10-K filings.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or announcement concluding its antitrust investigation into Nvidia by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or conclusion of its investigation by January 31, 2027, whatever it finds.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion ending its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or conclusion ending its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027, whatever the conclusion finds.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 9, 2026, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion ending it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority publish a decision or announcement concluding its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or announcement concluding the investigation by January 31, 2027, whether it takes action or closes the case without action.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t20\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the US government keep in force, broaden, or tighten its approval allowing Nvidia to sell some of its semiconductors to China under specified conditions, and at what scale will those permitted China sales occur?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether US export-control approval for Nvidia semiconductor sales to China remains in force, is expanded, or is restricted, and the resulting scale of Nvidia's permitted China sales.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal year ending late January 2027 (reported ~February 2027); set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision, checked against US export-control rule updates and Nvidia's China revenue disclosure.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"US Commerce Department/BIS export-control rule updates and licensing decisions, plus Nvidia's quarterly and annual filings disclosing China revenue.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Singapore seizes $42m mansion over Nvidia chip smuggling\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic names two tracked outcomes—the status of US export-control approval and the scale of Nvidia's permitted China sales—and neither is clearly the main one.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"By 2027-01-31, will a US export-control authorization remain in force that permits Nvidia to sell at least some semiconductors to China, as determined by US export-control rule updates and licensing decisions?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: On 2027-01-31, a US export-control authorization is in force that permits Nvidia to sell at least some semiconductors to China, whether under existing or revised conditions.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-02 and before 2027-01-31, the US Department of Commerce or BIS formally revokes or withdraws all authorization for Nvidia to sell semiconductors to China, or issues a rule prohibiting all such sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will the US export-control authorization allowing Nvidia to sell semiconductors to China under specified conditions remain in force, be broadened, or be tightened by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: By 2027-01-31, the authorization remains in force or has been broadened or tightened, including by being withdrawn.\",\n     \"No: Rung 1 does not hold on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t21\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity will NVIDIA have committed to AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support business model?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Total dollar amount of credit support / revenue-share-backed capacity NVIDIA has committed to AI cloud operators under the announced model, as disclosed in its filings.\",\n   \"period\": \"Next annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027, reported ~February 2027); set as the next annual report because the model is presented as already being introduced/underway.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (Form 10-K) and interim 10-Qs/8-Ks disclosing guarantees, credit support and revenue-share commitments to AI cloud partners.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   \"title\": \"NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What total USD amount of credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity has NVIDIA committed to AI cloud partners under this model by the FY2027 annual report, as disclosed in its filings?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 15,000,000,000 USD to below 50,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 50,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What total amount in USD of credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity has NVIDIA committed to AI cloud operators under its announced model, as disclosed in its FY2027 annual report?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 3,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 3,000,000,000 USD to below 7,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 7,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 15,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"As disclosed in NVIDIA's FY2027 annual report and related filings, what total USD amount of credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity will NVIDIA have committed to AI cloud operators by FY2027 year-end?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 3,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 3,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 10,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t22\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much credit support and revenue-share exposure will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners under its new AI-factory business model, and what contingent liability does that represent?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The amount of credit support/guarantees and revenue-share commitments NVIDIA discloses, and whether the exposure is material to its cash and credit risk.\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (Form 10-K) after the July 2026 announcement\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (Form 10-K), including its guarantees/contingent-liability and revenue-share disclosures\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   \"title\": \"NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What total dollar amount of credit support, guarantees, and revenue-share commitments to AI cloud partners does NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 25,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What total USD amount of NVIDIA's credit support, guarantees, and revenue-share commitments under the AI-cloud business model does NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K for the year ended 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 500,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 500,000,000 USD to below 2,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 2,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 10,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What total amount of credit support, guarantees, and revenue-share commitments under NVIDIA’s AI-cloud partner model does NVIDIA disclose for FY2027 in its annual report (Form 10-K)?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"Bearish: from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 25,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t23\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's U.S.-approved H200 chip sales to China translate into revenue-generating shipments by NVIDIA's fiscal year-end January 2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Chinese authorities permit H200 sales to Chinese commercial customers and NVIDIA records China data-center revenue from those shipments by the check date.\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal year-end (late January 2027), set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Chinese regulatory/import approval for H200 sales and NVIDIA's quarterly Form 10-Q/10-K disclosures or management commentary on China data-center revenue from H200 shipments.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA report or otherwise confirm in its Form 10-Q, Form 10-K, or management commentary that it recorded China data-center revenue from H200 shipments by January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA reports or otherwise confirms China data-center revenue from H200 shipments made by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Chinese authorities prohibit H200 sales to Chinese commercial customers, or NVIDIA formally abandons its plans to sell H200 chips to those customers. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA disclose by January 31, 2027, that it recognized China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA's Form 10-Q, Form 10-K, or management commentary confirms by January 31, 2027, that it recognized China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Chinese authorities formally prohibit H200 sales to Chinese commercial customers through January 31, 2027, or NVIDIA formally abandons plans to make those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA record China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers by January 31, 2027, as shown in its financial disclosures or management commentary?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA reports or comments that it recorded China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Chinese authorities formally prohibit H200 sales to Chinese commercial customers, or NVIDIA formally abandons its plan to make those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t24\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin AI chip platform begin shipping by the end of calendar 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin to customers, confirmed by NVIDIA.\",\n   \"period\": \"2026-12-31 (the item says shipping could begin later in 2026, from a 2026-07-02 article)\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's confirmation of first customer shipments of Vera Rubin, such as a press release, earnings call, or quarterly filing.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm that first shipments of its Vera Rubin AI chip platform to customers have begun by December 31, 2026, through a press release, earnings call, or quarterly filing?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA confirms that first shipments of Vera Rubin to customers have begun by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"Ruled out: NVIDIA formally announces after July 2, 2026, that it has canceled or abandoned the Vera Rubin platform before any first shipment to a customer. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm that it has made first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin AI chip platform by December 31, 2026?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA confirms first customer shipments of Vera Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"Ruled out: NVIDIA formally cancels Vera Rubin customer shipments for 2026 or announces that it will not ship Vera Rubin to customers by December 31, 2026. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm that Vera Rubin has begun shipping to customers by December 31, 2026? NVIDIA confirmation, such as a press release, earnings call, or quarterly filing, settles the question.\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA confirms that Vera Rubin has begun shipping to customers by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, NVIDIA announces that it has canceled Vera Rubin or that first customer shipments will begin after December 31, 2026. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t25\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the U.S. Commerce Department conclude its investigation into whether DeepSeek accessed restricted Nvidia AI chips and announce penalties or new export-control measures by NVIDIA's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A U.S. Commerce Department/Bureau of Industry and Security finding, penalty, or new export-control measure stemming from the investigation into DeepSeek's access to restricted Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-01-31 (NVIDIA's current fiscal year-end; set because the item reports a pending regulatory investigation with no date of its own)\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"U.S. Commerce Department/Bureau of Industry and Security public announcement, enforcement action, or Federal Register rule.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Singaporean Police Seize $42M Bungalow in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe - The Diplomat – Asia-Pacific Current Affairs Magazine\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will the U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security publicly issue a finding, impose a penalty, or announce a new export-control measure stemming from its investigation into whether DeepSeek accessed restricted Nvidia AI chips by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security publicly issues a finding, imposes a penalty, or announces a new export-control measure stemming from the investigation by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without issuing a finding, imposing a penalty, or announcing a new export-control measure stemming from it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will the U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security publicly announce a finding, penalty, or new export-control measure stemming from its investigation into DeepSeek’s access to restricted Nvidia chips by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security publicly announces a finding, penalty, or new export-control measure stemming from the investigation into DeepSeek’s access to restricted Nvidia chips by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without issuing a public finding, penalty, or new export-control measure. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will the U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security publicly announce a finding, impose a penalty, or announce a new export-control measure stemming from its investigation into whether DeepSeek accessed restricted Nvidia AI chips by 2027-01-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: The U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security publicly announces a finding, imposes a penalty, or announces a new export-control measure stemming from the investigation into whether DeepSeek accessed restricted Nvidia AI chips by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: The U.S. Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a finding, imposing a penalty, or announcing a new export-control measure stemming from it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t26\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend in combined data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The sum of calendar-2026 data center capex actually reported by the big four AI hyperscalers, versus the roughly $650 billion they are reported to plan for this year.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; settled by the four hyperscalers' full-year 2026 capex disclosures in their Q4 2026 earnings reports (January–February 2027), the release date of the quantity.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The four AI hyperscalers' quarterly earnings releases and annual 10-K filings reporting calendar-2026 capital expenditures.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-04\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"How much did the big four AI hyperscalers spend in combined data center capital expenditures during calendar 2026, according to their full-year 2026 capex disclosures?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers’ combined data center capital expenditures be for calendar 2026, as reported in their full-year 2026 earnings releases?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What was the combined data center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers in calendar 2026, as reported in their full-year 2026 earnings disclosures?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\\")\",\n     \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"800,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t27\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"What will NVIDIA's outstanding supply (purchase) commitments to its manufacturing and memory suppliers total at its next annual report?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The supply-commitments balance NVIDIA discloses in its next Form 10-K, versus the $119 billion reported in this item, and whether the obligation is growing faster than the revenue it supports (which would raise write-down or utilisation risk if hyperscaler orders slow).\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (Form 10-K, fiscal year ending late January 2027) — the next annual report for an obligation already undertaken, as section 3 fixes for such obligations.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's next Form 10-K (fiscal 2027), which discloses purchase/supply commitments outstanding, with the 10-Q filings in between as interim checks.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia’s Biggest Threat Is This: Everyone Is Desperate to Stop Paying Nvidia Prices.\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What total outstanding supply (purchase) commitments to manufacturing and memory suppliers will NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K, as stated in that filing?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 100,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 100,000,000,000 USD to below 115,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 115,000,000,000 USD to below 125,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Supply commitments of $119 billion\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 125,000,000,000 USD to below 140,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 140,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's outstanding supply (purchase) commitments to its manufacturing and memory suppliers be as of FY2027 year-end, as disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 90,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 90,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Supply commitments of $119 billion\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What amount of outstanding supply (purchase) commitments to manufacturing and memory suppliers will NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-04-01\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Strongly bullish: below 100,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Bullish: from 100,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \\\"Supply commitments of $119 billion\\\")\",\n     \"Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 145,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"Strongly bearish: 145,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t28\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin AI chip platform reach revenue-generating first shipments by the end of calendar 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Vera Rubin begins shipping in 2026, as the item reports it 'could begin shipping later this year'.\",\n   \"period\": \"End of calendar 2026 — the item states Vera Rubin is in full production and 'could begin shipping later this year' (2026); check date set at year-end 2026.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's quarterly results and Form 10-Q/10-K filings confirming Vera Rubin shipment/revenue recognition, and any official NVIDIA shipment announcement.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA make revenue-generating first shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by an official NVIDIA shipment announcement or company filing?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA makes revenue-generating first shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, confirmed by an official NVIDIA shipment announcement or company filing.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, NVIDIA formally announces that it has abandoned Vera Rubin or postponed its first shipments until after 2026. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping Vera Rubin by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by an official NVIDIA announcement or company filing?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA begins shipping Vera Rubin by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by an official NVIDIA announcement or company filing.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, NVIDIA announces that Vera Rubin shipments will not begin in calendar 2026 or formally abandons the Vera Rubin platform. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as shown by NVIDIA's quarterly results, SEC filings, or an official shipment announcement?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA begins shipping the Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by its quarterly results, SEC filings, or an official shipment announcement.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, NVIDIA announces that it has canceled any plan to begin Vera Rubin shipments in 2026 and will not begin shipping the platform until 2027 or later. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t29\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend in combined data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027, versus NVIDIA management's forecast that hyperscaler spending will top $1 trillion?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The sum of calendar-2027 data center capex actually reported by the big four AI hyperscalers, compared with the over-$1-trillion figure NVIDIA management forecast for 2027.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; settled by the four hyperscalers' full-year 2027 capex disclosures in their Q4 2027 earnings reports (January–February 2028), the release date of the quantity.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' full-year 2027 capital expenditure figures in their Q4 2027 earnings reports (Jan–Feb 2028).\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Below $200 Per Share Again. Here's When It Could Hit $300.\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What is the combined calendar-2027 data center capital expenditure of the four major AI hyperscalers, as reported in their full-year 2027 capex disclosures in their Q4 2027 earnings reports?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-03-30\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 800,000,000,000 USD to below 1,000,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 1,000,000,000,000 USD to below 1,200,000,000,000 USD: from 1,000,000,000,000 USD to below 1,200,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\\")\",\n     \"from 1,200,000,000,000 USD to below 1,500,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"1,500,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"What was the combined data-center capital expenditure of the four large AI hyperscalers in calendar 2027, as shown in their full-year 2027 capex disclosures in Q4 earnings reports?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-03-30\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 800,000,000,000 USD to below 950,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 950,000,000,000 USD to below 1,050,000,000,000 USD: from 950,000,000,000 USD to below 1,050,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\\")\",\n     \"from 1,050,000,000,000 USD to below 1,200,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"1,200,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What is the combined data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers in calendar 2027, as shown in their full-year 2027 capex disclosures in their Q4 2027 earnings reports?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-03-30\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 800,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 800,000,000,000 USD to below 950,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"from 950,000,000,000 USD to below 1,050,000,000,000 USD: from 950,000,000,000 USD to below 1,050,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\\")\",\n     \"from 1,050,000,000,000 USD to below 1,200,000,000,000 USD\",\n     \"1,200,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t30\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Vera CPU platform — the AI-workload server processor management introduced to push beyond GPUs — reach first customer shipments and begin generating revenue by Nvidia's fiscal year ending late January 2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments / initial revenue from Nvidia's Vera CPU platform, confirmed by the company.\",\n   \"period\": \"Nvidia's fiscal year ending late January 2027 (annual report ~February 2027); the item gives no shipment date for Vera CPU, so the check date is set at the current fiscal year-end because the item reports the processors are already being offered to cloud customers.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Nvidia's quarterly reports and earnings-call commentary disclosing Vera CPU sales or first customer shipments, plus any Nvidia shipment announcement for the Vera CPU platform.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-12\",\n   \"title\": \"Forget GPUs. Nvidia’s Next AI Gold Mine Could Be Even Bigger.\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm that its Vera CPU platform has entered customer commercialization—through first customer shipments or initial revenue—by FY2027 year-end (2027-01-31), as disclosed in its quarterly reports, earnings-call commentary, or a shipment announcement?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms by 2027-01-31 that Vera CPU has begun customer shipments or generated initial revenue.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-12, Nvidia formally abandons or discontinues the Vera CPU platform before any customer shipments or initial revenue, ruling out customer commercialization by 2027-01-31. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-12 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm that it made its first customer shipment of the Vera CPU platform by the end of FY2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that it made at least one customer shipment of the Vera CPU platform by 2027-01-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: Nvidia formally cancels or abandons the Vera CPU platform before 2027-01-31 without making a customer shipment. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-12 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm in its quarterly reports, earnings-call commentary, or a shipment announcement that Vera CPU has made its first customer shipments and begun generating revenue by FY2027 year-end, January 31, 2027?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that Vera CPU has made its first customer shipments and begun generating revenue by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 12, 2026, Nvidia formally abandons or cancels the Vera CPU platform before making any first customer shipments or generating any revenue from it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-12 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t31\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"What share of Chinese enterprises' AI accelerator spending will go to domestic suppliers (Huawei, Hygon, Cambricon and others) over the 12 months from mid-2026, and how far will Nvidia's share of the Chinese accelerator market fall from its present level?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The share of Chinese enterprises' AI accelerator budgets allocated to domestic products versus the ~30% baseline reported in the July 2026 Bloomberg Intelligence survey, and the direction of Nvidia's share of that market, as reported in follow-up surveys and Nvidia's disclosed China revenue.\",\n   \"period\": \"The 12 months following the survey's release on 2026-07-07 (through roughly mid-2027); set by the survey's stated 'next 12 months' horizon, checked against follow-up Bloomberg Intelligence surveys and Nvidia's quarterly China revenue disclosures over that window.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Follow-up Bloomberg Intelligence surveys of Chinese AI buyers, Chinese customs/import statistics for AI accelerators, domestic vendors' (Huawei, Hygon, Cambricon) reported revenue, and Nvidia's quarterly China revenue disclosure in its 10-Q filings.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-08\",\n   \"title\": \"Chinese companies are ditching Nvidia’s advanced accelerators for domestic AI suppliers\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked figure covers a rolling 12-month period, and neither the topic nor the item gives the publication day of the follow-up figure that would settle the outcome.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked figure covers a rolling 12-month period, and the topic and item do not give the publication day of the follow-up survey that would report the figure.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What percentage of Chinese enterprises’ AI accelerator budgets will be allocated to domestic products over the 12 months following the Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on 2026-07-07, as established by follow-up Bloomberg Intelligence surveys?\",\n    \"whose\": \"ai-capex\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 38 percent\",\n     \"from 38 percent to below 43 percent\",\n     \"from 43 percent to below 49 percent: from 43 percent to below 49 percent (the reference when the question opened: \\\"Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\\")\",\n     \"from 49 percent to below 54 percent\",\n     \"54 percent or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t32\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system begin shipping to customers by the end of calendar 2028, following SemiAnalysis's report that its debut slipped from 2027 to 2028 (which NVIDIA disputes, saying its roadmap is intact)?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments of the Kyber rack-scale architecture (NVL144) with Vera Rubin Ultra, confirmed by NVIDIA.\",\n   \"period\": \"2028-12-31 (the item says the Kyber debut was pushed to 2028 from a 2027 plan; the check date is the end of that year. If NVIDIA's 'roadmap is intact,' shipping in 2027 would also settle the by-end-2028 question affirmatively.)\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA confirmation of first shipments of Vera Rubin Ultra/Kyber systems to cloud customers, or an explicit product-timeline disclosure in NVIDIA's annual report or quarterly earnings materials.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-05\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm that first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin Ultra Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system have begun by December 31, 2028?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: By December 31, 2028, NVIDIA confirms that first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin Ultra Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system have begun.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 5, 2026 and before December 31, 2028, NVIDIA formally cancels the Vera Rubin Ultra Kyber NVL144 system or abandons plans to ship it to customers. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2028-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm that it has begun first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin Ultra Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system by 2028-12-31?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA confirms that first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin Ultra Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system have begun by 2028-12-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-05, NVIDIA formally cancels customer shipments of the Vera Rubin Ultra Kyber NVL144 system or formally discloses that they will not begin by 2028-12-31. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2028-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA confirm first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system by December 31, 2028?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA confirms first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system by December 31, 2028.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 5, 2026, NVIDIA formally cancels the Kyber NVL144 system or announces that it will not make first customer shipments by December 31, 2028. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2028-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t33\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"What will happen to HBM/DRAM contract prices over the 12 months to mid-2027, after rising roughly tenfold over the past year and becoming the data-center bottleneck?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The change in HBM/DRAM contract prices over the 12 months to mid-2027, versus the roughly tenfold rise over the prior year.\",\n   \"period\": \"The 12 months to 2027-06-30 (next calendar year); set from the item's report that memory prices rose tenfold over the past year and its view that conditions will persist absent an HBM breakthrough.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"TrendForce quarterly DRAM/HBM contract-price releases and Micron's quarterly HBM pricing and revenue disclosures through mid-2027.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia is a victim of the compute marketplace it created\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked figure covers a 12-month period ending 2027-06-30, not one fiscal or calendar year, and neither the topic nor the item gives the figure’s publication day.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The figure covers a rolling 12-month period ending 2027-06-30, and neither the topic nor the item gives the day that figure will be published.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked figure covers a rolling 12-month period to 2027-06-30, not one fiscal or calendar year, and neither the topic nor the item specifies the day that figure will be published.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t34\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's next-generation Vera Rubin AI chip platform reach first customer shipments — the step that brings its revenue — by the end of 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments / initial revenue from Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform, confirmed by the company.\",\n   \"period\": \"End of 2026 (item says Vera Rubin 'could begin shipping later this year'); checked against Nvidia's quarterly reports and management confirmation of initial Vera Rubin shipments.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Nvidia's quarterly earnings reports/filings and management commentary confirming initial Vera Rubin shipments and associated revenue.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia make first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed in Nvidia's quarterly reports, filings, or management commentary?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that it made first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Nvidia formally cancels or abandons the Vera Rubin platform before making any first customer shipments. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia make its first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed in Nvidia's quarterly reports, filings, or management commentary?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that it made its first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"Ruled out: Nvidia formally cancels the Vera Rubin platform or announces that it will make no customer shipments of the platform by December 31, 2026. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia make its first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026, as confirmed in its quarterly reports, filings, or management commentary?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that it has made its first customer shipments of the Vera Rubin platform by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Nvidia announces that it will make no Vera Rubin customer shipments by December 31, 2026, or formally abandons the Vera Rubin platform. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t35\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"What will the spot rental price of an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute average over calendar 2026, after peaking around $3.20/hour in May 2026 and then declining?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The realized spot rental price for an hour of H100 GPU time over calendar 2026, versus the ~$3.20/hour May 2026 peak.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (check date 2026-12-31); set from the item's reported May-2026 peak (~$3.20/hour) and subsequent decline in the H100 spot-rate series.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Ornn and other GPU compute marketplaces' published H100 spot-rate data (e.g., Ornn's index) covering calendar 2026.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia is a victim of the compute marketplace it created\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked matter is the H100 GPU compute spot rental price, which is not covered by any listed theme and is not a figure of NVDA itself.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The question is about the spot rental price of H100 GPU compute, a marketplace compute-service price not covered by any listed theme; it is not a figure of NVDA itself.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"What will the average spot rental price, in USD per hour of H100 GPU compute, be over calendar 2026, according to published H100 spot-rate data from Ornn or other GPU compute marketplaces?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 1\",\n     \"from 1 to below 1.5\",\n     \"from 1.5 to below 2: from 1.5 to below 2 (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 2 to below 2.5\",\n     \"2.5 or more\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t36\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the spot rental price of an NVIDIA H100 GPU-hour keep falling through calendar 2026, dropping below the ~$3.20/hour peak reached in May 2026, as custom accelerators and easing GPU supply pressure the market price of compute?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The trajectory of H100 GPU-hour spot rental prices (Ornn compute-marketplace index) over calendar 2026 — whether the rate continues to decline from the ~$3.20/hour May 2026 peak.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026 — checked against Ornn's published H100 spot rental-price index at year-end 2026.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Ornn's published spot-market H100 GPU-hour rental-price index (and comparable compute-marketplace price data) at year-end 2026.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia is a victim of the compute marketplace it created\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"What is Ornn's published H100 GPU-hour spot rental price, in USD per hour, measured on December 31, 2026?\",\n    \"whose\": \"semiconductor-cycle\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"below 1 USD\",\n     \"from 1 USD to below 2 USD\",\n     \"from 2 USD to below 3 USD: from 2 USD to below 3 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\",\n     \"from 3 USD to below 4 USD\",\n     \"4 USD or more\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The tracked matter is the spot rental price of H100 GPU-hours in the compute marketplace. It is not an NVIDIA figure, and none of the listed themes covers compute-market rental prices; custom silicon and AI capital spending are factors mentioned in the topic, not the tracked outcome.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will Ornn's published H100 GPU-hour spot rental-price index show the price continuing to decline from its approximately $3.20/hour May 2026 peak, with the year-end 2026 price below that peak?\",\n    \"whose\": \"custom-silicon\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: By December 31, 2026, Ornn's published H100 GPU-hour spot rental-price index shows a price below the approximately $3.20/hour May 2026 peak.\",\n     \"No: Rung 1 does not hold on 2026-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t37\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much will NVIDIA have invested in Firmus Technologies, and what equity stake will it hold, following its reported ~$500 million ($721 million) subscription to Firmus' $2.9 billion equity raising, once Firmus lists on the ASX?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The amount NVIDIA invests and the equity stake it holds in Firmus Technologies after its preference shares convert to ordinary equity at Firmus' ASX IPO.\",\n   \"period\": \"Firmus' ASX listing later in 2026 (preference shares convert to ordinary equity there); the stake is already undertaken, so it is also tracked by its amount at NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, expected early 2027). Set from the item's 'later this year' listing timing, within 18 months of the 2026-07-08 item.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Firmus Technologies' ASX listing prospectus and share register (its IPO later in 2026) and NVIDIA's next Form 10-K, disclosing NVIDIA's subscription and resulting stake.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-08\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia tips $720m into Firmus’ $2.9b raising; share split under way\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks both NVIDIA’s investment amount and its equity stake, and names neither as the main outcome.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks both NVIDIA’s investment amount and its resulting equity stake, with neither named as the main figure.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks two figures—the amount NVIDIA invests and its resulting equity stake in Firmus—and names neither as the main figure.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t38\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture, the rack system slated to debut with its Vera Rubin Ultra generation, reach first customer shipments, and in which year — 2027 as originally slated or 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments of Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 rack architecture (Vera Rubin Ultra generation), confirmed by the company, versus the reported more-than-12-month delay to 2028.\",\n   \"period\": \"2028 — the date SemiAnalysis reports for Kyber's delayed debut, against the original 2027 schedule stated in the item; checked against Nvidia's quarterly reports and management confirmation of initial Kyber/Rubin Ultra shipments.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"Nvidia's quarterly earnings reports and management statements confirming initial Kyber / Vera Rubin Ultra customer shipments (plus any product announcement or 8-K on the rack system).\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-05\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm that it has made first customer shipments of its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture for the Vera Rubin Ultra generation by 2028-12-31, in its quarterly reports or management statements?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that it has made first customer shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture for the Vera Rubin Ultra generation by 2028-12-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-05 and before 2028-12-31, Nvidia formally cancels the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture or formally abandons plans to make first customer shipments of it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2028-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm that it has made first customer shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture (Vera Rubin Ultra generation) by December 31, 2028, in a quarterly report, management statement, product announcement or 8-K?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that it has made first customer shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by December 31, 2028.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 5, 2026 and before December 31, 2028, Nvidia formally abandons or cancels the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture before making any first customer shipments. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2028-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will Nvidia confirm first customer shipments of its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture for the Vera Rubin Ultra generation by December 31, 2028?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: Nvidia confirms that first customer shipments of its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture for the Vera Rubin Ultra generation have occurred by December 31, 2028.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 5, 2026, Nvidia formally cancels or abandons the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture for the Vera Rubin Ultra generation without making first customer shipments. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2028-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"X\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t39\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"How much equity will NVIDIA hold in Intel, and at what total committed amount, at NVIDIA's next annual report, following its $5 billion equity investment in Intel?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The size and carrying amount of NVIDIA's equity stake in Intel, and any additional commitment, disclosed at NVIDIA's next annual report.\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, expected early 2027); the investment is already undertaken, so it is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (Form 10-K) and any Schedule 13D/13G or other SEC filings disclosing its Intel equity stake and committed amount.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-01\",\n   \"title\": \"Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks several figures—the size of NVIDIA’s equity stake, its carrying amount, and any additional commitment—without naming one as the main figure.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic tracks several figures—the size of NVIDIA’s equity stake, its carrying amount, and any additional commitment—without naming one as the main figure.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"declined\": \"The topic's outcome names several tracked quantities—the size of NVIDIA's Intel stake, its carrying amount, and any additional commitment—without identifying one as the main figure.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Z\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"t40\",\n  \"topic\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture, designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips, reach revenue-generating first shipments in calendar 2027 as originally planned, or slip to 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether the Kyber rack debuts and ships with Vera Rubin Ultra in calendar 2027 (consistent with NVIDIA's 'roadmap is intact') or is delayed to 2028 (SemiAnalysis), and when first shipments actually occur.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 first shipments — the item says Kyber 'had been slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra ... in 2027' and reports a >12-month delay to 2028; whether 2027 shipments occur can be checked at year-end 2027, with 2028 as the reported slip date.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's shipment confirmations and product launch announcements, quarterly earnings-call commentary/10-Q revenue timing for Rubin Ultra/Kyber, or independent confirmation of rack deployments.\"\n  },\n  \"opening_article\": {\n   \"date\": \"2026-07-05\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\"\n  },\n  \"attempts\": [\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA make first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack with Vera Rubin Ultra during calendar 2027, as determined by NVIDIA shipment confirmations, earnings-call disclosures, or independently confirmed customer deployments?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA makes first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack with Vera Rubin Ultra by 2027-12-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-05, NVIDIA announces that it has canceled Kyber or formally deferred its first shipments with Vera Rubin Ultra until 2028. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 2,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA make its first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack system with Vera Rubin Ultra by December 31, 2027, as verifiable through NVIDIA shipment disclosures, earnings-call or filing disclosures, or independently confirmed deployments?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA makes its first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack system with Vera Rubin Ultra by December 31, 2027, as confirmed by NVIDIA disclosures or independently confirmed deployments.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After July 5, 2026, NVIDIA formally cancels Kyber or announces that its first shipments will not occur before 2028. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"attempt\": 3,\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA make Kyber NVL144's first revenue-generating shipments with Vera Rubin Ultra in calendar 2027, as established by NVIDIA shipment confirmations, product announcements, earnings-call commentary or filings, or independent confirmation of deployments?\",\n    \"whose\": \"NVDA\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"answer_choices\": [\n     \"Yes: NVIDIA makes Kyber NVL144's first revenue-generating shipments with Vera Rubin Ultra by 2027-12-31.\",\n     \"Ruled out: After 2026-07-05, NVIDIA announces that it has cancelled Kyber NVL144 or formally moved its first revenue-generating shipments with Vera Rubin Ultra to after calendar 2027. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n     \"Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-12-31.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"run\": \"Y\"\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
