{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/july-topics-packet.json\\\"));\nfor x in p:\n print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"run\\\"],x[\\\"topic\\\"][\\\"description\\\"],\\\"|\\\",x[\\\"opening_article\\\"][\\\"title\\\"])\n for a in x[\\\"attempts\\\"]:\n  print(a[\\\"attempt\\\"],a.get(\\\"question\\\", \\\"DECLINED: \\\"+a.get(\\\"declined\\\",\\\"\\\")), a.get(\\\"whose\\\",\\\"\\\"),a.get(\\\"due_day\\\",\\\"\\\"), \\\"|\\\", \\\"; \\\".join(a.get(\\\"answer_choices\\\",[])) if a[\\\"attempt\\\"]==1 else \\\"\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"\n t01 Z How much will U.S. federal agencies obligate in AI-related spending in calendar/fiscal 2026, and how much in new AI-related contract awards will be recorded? | FBI Issues RFI for AI Supercomputers Featuring Nvidia B300 GPUs and Google TPUs\n1 DECLINED: The topic tracks two figures—2026 AI-related federal spending obligations and potential AI contract awards—and neither is identified as the main figure.   | \n2 DECLINED: The topic names two figures—AI-related federal spending obligations and potential AI contract awards—and neither is identified as the main one.   | \n3 DECLINED: The topic tracks two figures—total AI-related spending obligated and the value of potential AI contract awards—and neither is identified as the main figure.   | \n\n t02 X Will the combined data center capital expenditures of the 'big four' AI hyperscalers for calendar 2026 come in near the ~$650 billion the item reports they plan to spend? | Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\n1 What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditure be for calendar 2026, as measured by summing the capex lines in their Q4 2026 earnings reports? ai-capex 2027-03-31 | below 500,000,000,000 USD; from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD; from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\"); from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD; 800,000,000,000 USD or more\n2 What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be for calendar 2026, as measured by the sum of their capital-expenditure lines in their Q4 2026 earnings reports? ai-capex 2027-03-31 | \n3 How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend in aggregate on data center capital expenditures during calendar 2026, according to the capital expenditure lines in their Q4 2026 earnings reports? ai-capex 2027-03-31 | \n\n t03 Z Will China's government permit NVIDIA to sell its H200 AI chips to Chinese customers, lifting its current block, by NVIDIA's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31? | Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case\n1 Will China's government or a regulator permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips to Chinese customers by 2027-01-31, as shown by an official Chinese decision or NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments or revenue to Chinese customers? chip-export-controls 2027-01-31 | Yes: By 2027-01-31, an official Chinese government or regulator decision permits H200 sales to Chinese customers, or NVIDIA confirms H200 shipments or revenue to Chinese customers.; Ruled out: The Chinese government or a Chinese regulator formally denies permission for H200 sales to Chinese customers or formally prohibits those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.; Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\n2 Will China permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips to Chinese customers by 2027-01-31, as evidenced by an official Chinese decision or NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments or revenue to Chinese customers? chip-export-controls 2027-01-31 | \n3 Will China officially permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips to Chinese customers by 2027-01-31, as established by an official Chinese decision or NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments or revenue to those customers? chip-export-controls 2027-01-31 | \n\n t04 Z Will France's competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets and issue a decision (fines or remedies) by Nvidia's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31? | Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\n1 Will the French competition authority publish a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets by 2027-01-31? NVDA 2027-01-31 | Yes: The French competition authority publishes a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets by 2027-01-31.; Ruled out: After 2026-07-09, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a final decision. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.; Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\n2 Will the French competition authority publish a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by 2027-01-31? NVDA 2027-01-31 | \n3 Will the French competition authority publish a final decision on its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by 2027-01-31? NVDA 2027-01-31 | \n\n t05 X How large will NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments be at its next annual report, and could that obligation pressure its cash or credit position if AI demand disappoints? | How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\n1 What total dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments outstanding at the end of FY2027 will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K? NVDA 2027-04-01 | Strongly bullish: below 90,000,000,000 USD; Bullish: from 90,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD; Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \"$119B in supply commitments\"); Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD; Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\n2 What total dollar amount of NVIDIA supply purchase commitments will be disclosed in its Form 10-K for FY2027? NVDA 2027-04-01 | \n3 What total dollar amount of NVIDIA supply purchase commitments will NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 annual report, as measured in the report’s purchase commitments / contractual obligations disclosure? NVDA 2027-04-01 | \n\n t06 X How large will US federal AI spending obligations be in calendar 2026, and how much in potential contract awards, as a demand pool for Nvidia's AI accelerators? | FBI Issues RFI for AI Supercomputers Featuring Nvidia B300 GPUs and Google TPUs\n1 What were total US federal AI spending obligations in calendar 2026, according to year-end 2026 federal procurement data from USAspending.gov and SAM.gov? ai-capex 2027-03-31 | below 3,000,000,000 USD; from 3,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD; from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \"$7.2 billion\"); from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD; 15,000,000,000 USD or more\n2 What total amount of US federal AI spending obligations will year-end 2026 federal procurement data (USAspending.gov/SAM.gov) show for calendar 2026? ai-capex 2027-03-31 | \n3 DECLINED: no ladder: refused   | \n\n t07 X How large is NVIDIA's equity investment in Intel, and will the $5 billion stake be completed and held at that level