d for AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model, as measured on 2027-12-31, according to NVIDIA's annual report, Form 10-K, Form 8-K, other filing disclosures, or signed partner agreements? NVDA 2027-12-31 | \n3 What aggregate USD amount of credit-support, guarantee, or similar credit-enhancement commitments will NVIDIA have signed for AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model by 2027-12-31, as determined from signed partner agreements and NVIDIA filings? NVDA 2027-12-31 | \n\n t11 Z How much will NVIDIA have outstanding in supply/purchase commitments at its next annual report? | Nvidia’s Biggest Threat Is This: Everyone Is Desperate to Stop Paying Nvidia Prices.\n1 What dollar amount of NVIDIA’s supply, purchase and capacity commitments will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K? NVDA 2027-04-01 | Strongly bullish: below 90,000,000,000 USD; Bullish: from 90,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD; Neutral: from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 130,000,000,000 USD (the amount last reported when the question opened: \"Supply commitments of $119 billion\"); Bearish: from 130,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD; Strongly bearish: 150,000,000,000 USD or more\n2 What dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply and purchase/capacity commitments will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K? NVDA 2027-04-01 | \n3 What dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply commitments (purchase and capacity commitments) will be disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K contractual-obligations disclosure? NVDA 2027-04-01 | \n\n t12 Y Will the French competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA's cloud-AI and GPU practices and impose remedies or fines, and by when? | Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\n1 Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion resolving its investigation into NVIDIA by January 31, 2027? NVDA 2027-01-31 | Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or conclusion resolving its investigation into NVIDIA by January 31, 2027, whatever it finds.; Ruled out: The French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion resolving it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.; Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\n2 Will the French competition authority publish a decision or announcement concluding or resolving its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA's cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027? NVDA 2027-01-31 | \n3 Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion resolving its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA by 2027-01-31? NVDA 2027-01-31 | \n\n t13 X Will China's government allow selected Chinese AI firms (including Alibaba Group Holding) to buy Nvidia H200 GPUs, and at what scale, replacing the current restriction that bars Chinese firms from purchasing the device? | Game-changer? Why China is finally letting its AI firms buy the Nvidia H200\n1 Will the Chinese government officially authorize selected Chinese AI firms, including Alibaba, to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs by January 31, 2027? chip-export-controls 2027-01-31 | Yes: By January 31, 2027, the Chinese government officially authorizes selected Chinese AI firms, including Alibaba, to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs.; Ruled out: After July 9, 2026, the Chinese government formally announces that it will not authorize selected Chinese AI firms to purchase Nvidia H200 GPUs, or formally abandons the reported plan to authorize those purchases. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, a