2028-12-31.\n2 Will Nvidia confirm that it has made first customer shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture (Vera Rubin Ultra generation) by December 31, 2028, in a quarterly report, management statement, product announcement or 8-K? NVDA 2028-12-31 | \n3 Will Nvidia confirm first customer shipments of its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture for the Vera Rubin Ultra generation by December 31, 2028? NVDA 2028-12-31 | \n\n t39 Z How much equity will NVIDIA hold in Intel, and at what total committed amount, at NVIDIA's next annual report, following its $5 billion equity investment in Intel? | Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC\n1 DECLINED: The topic tracks several figures—the size of NVIDIA’s equity stake, its carrying amount, and any additional commitment—without naming one as the main figure.   | \n2 DECLINED: The topic tracks several figures—the size of NVIDIA’s equity stake, its carrying amount, and any additional commitment—without naming one as the main figure.   | \n3 DECLINED: The topic's outcome names several tracked quantities—the size of NVIDIA's Intel stake, its carrying amount, and any additional commitment—without identifying one as the main figure.   | \n\n t40 Y Will NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture, designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips, reach revenue-generating first shipments in calendar 2027 as originally planned, or slip to 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports? | Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\n1 Will NVIDIA make first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack with Vera Rubin Ultra during calendar 2027, as determined by NVIDIA shipment confirmations, earnings-call disclosures, or independently confirmed customer deployments? NVDA 2027-12-31 | Yes: NVIDIA makes first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack with Vera Rubin Ultra by 2027-12-31.; Ruled out: After 2026-07-05, NVIDIA announces that it has canceled Kyber or formally deferred its first shipments with Vera Rubin Ultra until 2028. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.; Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-12-31.\n2 Will NVIDIA make its first shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack system with Vera Rubin Ultra by December 31, 2027, as verifiable through NVIDIA shipment disclosures, earnings-call or filing disclosures, or independently confirmed deployments? NVDA 2027-12-31 | \n3 Will NVIDIA make Kyber NVL144's first revenue-generating shipments with Vera Rubin Ultra in calendar 2027, as established by NVIDIA shipment confirmations, product announcements, earnings-call commentary or filings, or independent confirmation of deployments? NVDA 2027-12-31 | \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/july-topics-packet.json\\\"));\nfor x in p[17:24]:\n print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"run\\\"],x[\\\"topic\\\"][\\\"description\\\"],\\\"|\\\",x[\\\"opening_article\\\"][\\\"title\\\"])\n for a in x[\\\"attempts\\\"]: print(a[\\\"attempt\\\"],a.get(\\\"question\\\", \\\"DECLINED: \\\"+a.get(\\\"declined\\\",\\\"\\\")),a.get(\\\"whose\\\",\\\"\\\"),a.get(\\\"due_day\\\",\\\"\\\"), a.get(\\\"answer_choices\\\",[]))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/july-topics-packet.json\\\"));\nfor x in p[17:24]:\n print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"run\\\"],x[\\\"topic\\\"][\\\"description\\\"],\\\"|\\\",x[\\\"opening_article\\\"][\\\"title\\\"])\n for a in x[\\\"attempts\\\"]: print(a[\\\"attempt\\\"],a.get(\\\"question\\\", \\\"DECLINED: \\\"+a.get(\\\"declined\\\",\\\"\\\")),a.get(\\\"whose\\\",\\\"\\\"),a.get(\\\"due_day\\\",\\\"\\\"), a.get(\\\"answer_choices\\\",[]))'\"","aggregated_output":"\n t18 Y How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026, and does the aggregate reach the ~$650 billion currently planned? | Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\n1 How much did Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet and Meta report spending on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026, as disclosed in their full-year 2026 earnings releases? ai-capex 2027-03-31 ['below 500,000,000,000 USD', 'from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD', 'from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\")', 'from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD', '800,000,000,000 USD or more']\n2 What will the combined data-center capital expenditures actually reported or spent by Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, and Meta be for calendar 2026, as disclosed in their full-year 2026 earnings releases? ai-capex 2027-03-31 ['below 500,000,000,000 USD', 'from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD', 'from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \"around $650 billion\")', 'from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD', '800,000,000,000 USD or more']\n3 What will Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, and Meta's combined data-center capital expenditures actually reported or spent be for calendar 2026, according to their full-year 2026 capex disclosures in their Q4 2026 earnings releases? ai-capex 2027-03-31 ['below 500,000,000,000 USD', 'from 500,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD', 'from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD: from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \"plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\")', 'from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 800,000,000,000 USD', '800,000,000,000 USD or more']\n\n t19 X Will France's competition authority (Autorité de la concurrence) conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices by issuing a formal decision — a statement of objections, fine or behavioural remedies — rather than closing the case without action? | Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\n1 Will the French competition authority publish a decision or announcement concluding its antitrust investigation into Nvidia by January 31, 2027? NVDA 2027-01-31 ['Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or conclusion of its investigation by January 31, 2027, whatever it finds.', 'Ruled out: The French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.']\n2 Will the French competition authority publish a decision or conclusion ending its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027? NVDA 2027-01-31 ['Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or conclusion ending its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027, whatever the conclusion finds.', 'Ruled out: After July 9, 2026, the French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion ending it. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.']\n3 Will the French competition authority publish a decision or announcement concluding its antitrust investigation into Nvidia’s cloud-AI and GPU practices by January 31, 2027? NVDA 2027-01-31 ['Yes: The French competition authority publishes a decision or announcement concluding the investigation by January 31, 2027, whether it takes action or closes the case without action.', 'Ruled out: The French competition authority formally abandons or withdraws the investigation without publishing a decision or conclusion. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-09 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.']\n\n t20 X Will the US government keep in force, broaden, or tighten its approval allowing Nvidia to sell some of its semiconductors to China under specified conditions, and at what scale will those permitted China sales occur? | Singapore seizes $42m mansion over Nvidia chip smuggling\n1 DECLINED: The topic names two tracked outcomes—the status of US export-control approval and the scale of Nvidia's permitted China sales—and neither is clearly the main one.   []\n2 By 2027-01-31, will a US export-control authorization remain in force that permits Nvidia to sell at least some semiconductors to China, as determined by US export-control rule updates and licensing decisions? chip-export-controls 2027-01-31 ['Yes: On 2027-01-31, a US export-control authorization is in force that permits Nvidia to sell at least some semiconductors to China, whether under existing or revised conditions.', 'Ruled out: After 2026-07-02 and before 2027-01-31, the US Department of Commerce or BIS formally revokes or withdraws all authorization for Nvidia to sell semiconductors to China, or issues a rule prohibiting all such sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.']\n3 Will the US export-control authorization allowing Nvidia to sell semiconductors to China under specified conditions remain in force, be broadened, or be tightened by 2027-01-31? chip-export-controls 2027-01-31 ['Yes: By 2027-01-31, the authorization remains in force or has been broadened or tightened, including by being withdrawn.', 'No: Rung 1 does not hold on 2027-01-31.']\n\n t21 X How much credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity will NVIDIA have committed to AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support business model? | NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog\n1 What total USD amount of credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity has NVIDIA committed to AI cloud partners under this model by the FY2027 annual report, as disclosed in its filings? NVDA 2027-04-01 ['Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD', 'Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD', 'Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)', 'Bearish: from 15,000,000,000 USD to below 50,000,000,000 USD', 'Strongly bearish: 50,000,000,000 USD or more']\n2 What total amount in USD of credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity has NVIDIA committed to AI cloud operators under its announced model, as disclosed in its FY2027 annual report? NVDA 2027-04-01 ['Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD', 'Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 3,000,000,000 USD', 'Neutral: from 3,000,000,000 USD to below 7,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)', 'Bearish: from 7,000,000,000 USD to below 15,000,000,000 USD', 'Strongly bearish: 15,000,000,000 USD or more']\n3 As disclosed in NVIDIA's FY2027 annual report and related filings, what total USD amount of credit support and revenue-share-backed capacity will NVIDIA have committed to AI cloud operators by FY2027 year-end? NVDA 2027-04-01 ['Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD', 'Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 3,000,000,000 USD', 'Neutral: from 3,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)', 'Bearish: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD', 'Strongly bearish: 10,000,000,000 USD or more']\n\n t22 Y How much credit support and revenue-share exposure will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners under its new AI-factory business model, and what contingent liability does that represent? | NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog\n1 What total dollar amount of credit support, guarantees, and revenue-share commitments to AI cloud partners does NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K? NVDA 2027-04-01 ['Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD', 'Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD', 'Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)', 'Bearish: from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD', 'Strongly bearish: 25,000,000,000 USD or more']\n2 What total USD amount of NVIDIA's credit support, guarantees, and revenue-share commitments under the AI-cloud business model does NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K for the year ended 2027-01-31? NVDA 2027-04-01 ['Strongly bullish: below 500,000,000 USD', 'Bullish: from 500,000,000 USD to below 2,000,000,000 USD', 'Neutral: from 2,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)', 'Bearish: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD', 'Strongly bearish: 10,000,000,000 USD or more']\n3 What total amount of credit support, guarantees, and revenue-share commitments under NVIDIA’s AI-cloud partner model does NVIDIA disclose for FY2027 in its annual report (Form 10-K)? NVDA 2027-04-01 ['Strongly bullish: below 1,000,000,000 USD', 'Bullish: from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD', 'Neutral: from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)', 'Bearish: from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD', 'Strongly bearish: 25,000,000,000 USD or more']\n\n t23 Y Will NVIDIA's U.S.-approved H200 chip sales to China translate into revenue-generating shipments by NVIDIA's fiscal year-end January 2027? | Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case\n1 Will NVIDIA report or otherwise confirm in its Form 10-Q, Form 10-K, or management commentary that it recorded China data-center revenue from H200 shipments by January 31, 2027? NVDA 2027-01-31 ['Yes: NVIDIA reports or otherwise confirms China data-center revenue from H200 shipments made by January 31, 2027.', 'Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Chinese authorities prohibit H200 sales to Chinese commercial customers, or NVIDIA formally abandons its plans to sell H200 chips to those customers. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.']\n2 Will NVIDIA disclose by January 31, 2027, that it recognized China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers? NVDA 2027-01-31 [\"Yes: NVIDIA's Form 10-Q, Form 10-K, or management commentary confirms by January 31, 2027, that it recognized China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers.\", 'Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Chinese authorities formally prohibit H200 sales to Chinese commercial customers through January 31, 2027, or NVIDIA formally abandons plans to make those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.']\n3 Will NVIDIA record China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers by January 31, 2027, as shown in its financial disclosures or management commentary? NVDA 2027-01-31 ['Yes: NVIDIA reports or comments that it recorded China data-center revenue from H200 shipments to Chinese commercial customers by January 31, 2027.', 'Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, Chinese authorities formally prohibit H200 sales to Chinese commercial customers, or NVIDIA formally abandons its plan to make those sales. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.']\n\n t24 Z Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin AI chip platform begin shipping by the end of calendar 2026? | Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\n1 Will NVIDIA confirm that first shipments of its Vera Rubin AI chip platform to customers have begun by December 31, 2026, through a press release, earnings call, or quarterly filing? NVDA 2026-12-31 ['Yes: NVIDIA confirms that first shipments of Vera Rubin to customers have begun by December 31, 2026.', 'Ruled out: NVIDIA formally announces after July 2, 2026, that it has canceled or abandoned the Vera Rubin platform before any first shipment to a customer. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.']\n2 Will NVIDIA confirm that it has made first customer shipments of its Vera Rubin AI chip platform by December 31, 2026? NVDA 2026-12-31 ['Yes: NVIDIA confirms first customer shipments of Vera Rubin by December 31, 2026.', 'Ruled out: NVIDIA formally cancels Vera Rubin customer shipments for 2026 or announces that it will not ship Vera Rubin to customers by December 31, 2026. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.']\n3 Will NVIDIA confirm that Vera Rubin has begun shipping to customers by December 31, 2026? NVIDIA confirmation, such as a press release, earnings call, or quarterly filing, settles the question. NVDA 2026-12-31 ['Yes: NVIDIA confirms that Vera Rubin has begun shipping to customers by December 31, 2026.', 'Ruled out: After July 2, 2026, NVIDIA announces that it has canceled Vera Rubin or that first customer shipments will begin after December 31, 2026. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2026-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.', 'Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
